course: dictionary
lesson: 5769
title: Lunchtime: a time and a break
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Lunchtime is a noun. It names a time, the middle of the day when people eat lunch, and at school it also names the break for eating and playing. You can often tell which meaning is used from the words around it. «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match» is about a game played in the break, so lunchtime is the school break here.
explain: The word can be used with other words to make phrases. «By lunchtime she has written a story» means the story was finished before or at the middle of the day. Ask yourself: what does lunchtime mean in this sentence? Then check by swapping in your meaning and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Some clues tell you lunchtime is a break at school. «A boy in Texas kept cheating in games at break time; soon nobody wanted to play with him, and he spent lunchtimes alone.» The words break time sit right beside lunchtimes, so they help you work out its meaning.
fact: Lunchtime is a noun. It means the time in the middle of the day when people eat lunch.
fact: At school, lunchtime is the break in the middle of the day for eating and playing outside.
fact: The plural is lunchtimes, as in «he spent lunchtimes alone».
fact: Phrases with lunchtime include at lunchtime, by lunchtime, lunchtime club and lunchtime supervisor.
fact: Lunchtime is one word made from two words, lunch and time.
exercise: «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» What is a lunchtime match? | A match played only on Saturdays | A match played late at night | *A match played in the middle-of-the-day break | A match with no goals
exercise: In «he spent lunchtimes alone», which words help you guess that lunchtimes means school breaks? | Texas | alone | cheating | *break time
exercise: Jade asks, «What is a lunchtime club?» Which answer is right? | A club for grown-ups who cook lunch | A club that sells sandwiches to parents | A club that only meets in July | *A club that meets at lunchtime
test: «By lunchtime she has written a story about a dragon.» What does by lunchtime mean here? | *Up to the middle of the day | At the very end of the week | After school has finished | Late at night
test: School starts the lunch break at 12:00 and it ends at 12:45. How long is lunchtime? | 30 minutes | 1 hour and 45 minutes | *45 minutes | 15 minutes
exam: Which word is the plural of lunchtime? | lunchtimey | lunchtime's | lunchtimed | *lunchtimes
